eloper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3\\,\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}=3\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $6x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3\\int \\frac{1}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4207968f4e09770be703843106668d261c81eac2351ac6724a5e99fb8a907a0b" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(36x)}{6}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{2}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{36}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{arcsec}(36x)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡($\n{{field-1}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/12)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/12}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{12})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{12}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{12}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{12}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{12})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{12}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4207968f4e09770be703843106668d261c81eac2351ac6724a5e99fb8a907a0b" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "5be80e63c137299d0e0e83f45d30b5b214033124967e6b35eaa2c212dc23562f" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{9}{4\\sqrt{1-9x^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-470.json" "file_sha256" "1435394612aecb48eb059230fa8b1c3c746e91a96bae660cc7ef755955f4e4c4" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\textrm{d}u = \\arcsin(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $9x^2 = (3x)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\,\\textrm d u=\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{4\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{9}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3x)^{2}}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-470.json" "file_sha256" "1435394612aecb48eb059230fa8b1c3c746e91a96bae660cc7ef755955f4e4c4" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral  $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-471.json" "file_sha256" "a975caa500c4657b7f477c9ceb80ab5761d91a2717f5f9ceac15f087b25261ec" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\int \\dfrac{3}{2(1 + 25x^2)} = \\dfrac 3 2 \\int \\dfrac{1}{1+25x^2}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^2}\\textrm{d}u =\\arctan u +C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $25x^2 = (5x)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 5\\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{2+50{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(5x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡5x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-471.json" "file_sha256" "a975caa500c4657b7f477c9ceb80ab5761d91a2717f5f9ceac15f087b25261ec" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{5\\, \\textrm{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^2-1}}  = }$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-5014.json" "file_sha256" "35f9523f03b71884abfc10e15c0a26d9f10bcb0587c6a3ed222655da25b76ee8" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This resembles the basic integral for $\\textrm{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^2-1}} \\textrm{d}u = \\textrm{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nLet $u = 5x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n5\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5\\,\\text{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}} & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-5014.json" "file_sha256" "35f9523f03b71884abfc10e15c0a26d9f10bcb0587c6a3ed222655da25b76ee8" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt 2} \\dfrac{1}{2+x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-472.json" "file_sha256" "6971fcf80e5ddd49db1502806ec3e5d5058537acead60eadae43d95f96e66011" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+{x}^{2}/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that this integral now resembles the basic integral for the inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int\\dfrac{1}{1+u^2}\\,\\textrm d u = \\arctan{u} + C.\n$$\n\nWe make the substitution $u=\\dfrac{x}{\\sqrt 2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\sqrt 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-472.json" "file_sha256" "6971fcf80e5ddd49db1502806ec3e5d5058537acead60eadae43d95f96e66011" "basis" 1748 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8}{16+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070130/state.json" "file_sha256" "e59e1b71ebf7bfe048ef53492dc8da7d2a847c534494f986e3832cfb56182984" "basis" 2451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{16+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{16\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/16)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/16}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{16+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070130/state.json" "file_sha256" "e59e1b71ebf7bfe048ef53492dc8da7d2a847c534494f986e3832cfb56182984" "basis" 2451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070130/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070130/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f3f83d31ee83f1ca04a6e320b749858f9722b2eef55e8a68246d76daab823e95" "basis" 2451 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/m