ibute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081876/state.json" "file_sha256" "e7bbb47845a2e23b35f5040b32279d278f6ed5a78c9f14e4c24c773a7367c5df"} {"question" "q-2506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081876/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d6962be85cd3228234bebdeaf5b79a516623b560a0cec1cb2afbcf673404b4f"} {"question" "q-2506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081876/state.json" "file_sha256" "e7bbb47845a2e23b35f5040b32279d278f6ed5a78c9f14e4c24c773a7367c5df"} {"question" "q-2506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)}{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)}{9}