qrt{49-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081876/state.json" "file_sha256" "e7bbb47845a2e23b35f5040b32279d278f6ed5a78c9f14e4c24c773a7367c5df"} {"question" "q-49547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{49-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{49\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/49)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/49}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/7)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{7})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{7}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{7}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=7\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{49-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{7}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/7)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (7\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x}{7})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081876/state.json" "file_sha256" "e7bbb47845a2e23b35f5040b32279d278f6ed5a78c9f14e4c24c773a7367c5df"} {"question" "q-49547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081876/activity-metad