{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081876/state.json" "file_sha256" "e7bbb47845a2e23b35f5040b32279d278f6ed5a78c9f14e4c24c773a7367c5df"} {"question" "q-49548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081876/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d6962be85cd3228234bebdeaf5b79a516623b560a0cec1cb2afbcf673404b4f"} {"question" "q-49548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081876/state.json" "file_sha256" "e7bbb47845a2e23b35f5040b32279d278f6ed5a78c9f14e4c24c773a7367c5df"} {"question" "q-49548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{